{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":30000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-opus-5-5","packSha":"a068e0aae42fb19c54f3c5f8fb74cd8a47fafca6c46c7c57cc539c2085eb59a8","packTokens":12422,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":255,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"intent","tokens":528,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":705,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"assumptions","tokens":1692,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"cb","tokens":341,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"spec","tokens":8786,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":7,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"critic"},"pointers":[],"system":"Adversarial reviewer. Find defects in this spec; don't praise; don't rewrite it.\nRubric: 1 conflicts between requirements 2 missing error, empty and permission paths 3 ACs not observable at a public surface 4 scope creep beyond the intent 5 claims about existing behaviour without anchors 6 state transitions and existing data 7 behaviour changes outside the requested scope (blast radius) 8 hardcoded identifiers that should be configuration.\nEach finding: rubric number, reqId, severity (critical|high|medium|low), one-sentence evidence in \"finding\". Empty list if none.\nThe human answered questions and accepted assumptions (below). Scope they decided is not a defect: don't flag it.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"intent\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"changeClass\": \"feature\",\n \"header\": {\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-30T20:46:31.819Z\",\n  \"inputsHash\": \"\",\n  \"kind\": \"intent\",\n  \"producedBy\": {\n   \"model\": \"claude-haiku-4-5\",\n   \"stage\": \"intake\"\n  },\n  \"runId\": \"20260930-invoice-reminders-a-small-4006\",\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1\n },\n \"rigor\": \"full\",\n \"risk\": \"high\",\n \"riskTags\": [\n  \"public-api\",\n  \"auth\",\n  \"payments\",\n  \"pii\"\n ],\n \"source\": \"cli\",\n \"spans\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-1\",\n   \"text\": \"When an invoice is 7 days past its due date, the system shall mark it overdue and show it on the overdue list\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-2\",\n   \"text\": \"When staff press 'Send reminder' on an overdue invoice, the system shall email the customer a reminder with the invoice number, amount and due date\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-3\",\n   \"text\": \"The system shall record each reminder sent, with who sent it and when, and show the history on the invoice\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-4\",\n   \"text\": \"If an email cannot be delivered, the system shall show the failure on the invoice and keep it on the overdue list\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-5\",\n   \"text\": \"Staff shall be able to filter the overdue list by customer and by days overdue\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-6\",\n   \"text\": \"Build overdue list screen (table, filters, a 'Send reminder' button per row)\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-7\",\n   \"text\": \"Build invoice detail screen (amount, due date, reminder history, delivery failures)\"\n  }\n ],\n \"touchesUi\": true\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Who can view the screens and send reminders, and how do staff sign in?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Any authenticated staff user, using the existing API's authentication\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Which email address receives the reminder, and what happens if the customer has several contacts or none?\",\n  \"answer\": \"The customer's single billing email from the existing record; if missing, the send is blocked with an error\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"Can reminder history entries be edited or deleted?\",\n  \"answer\": \"No, they are append-only and immutable\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Payments are out of scope. So how does an invoice come off the overdue list once it is paid or closed?\",\n  \"answer\": \"The existing system's invoice status (paid/cancelled) is read and closed invoices drop off automatically\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"How should repeated sends be guarded against?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Disable the button while a send is in progress only\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Is 'overdue' a status saved on the invoice (for example by a daily job), or is it worked out from the due date each time the list loads?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Computed at query time from due date and today's date\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"Where are reminder history records stored, given that invoices live in the client's existing system?\",\n  \"answer\": \"New table in the same Postgres database, referencing invoice ID\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"Is a failed send recorded in the append-only reminder history, and does a later successful send clear the failure shown on the invoice?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Every attempt (success or failure) is a history entry; the latest status is shown\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"assumptions\" kind=\"assumptions\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\",\n   \"I-6\",\n   \"I-7\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-1\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"Where do invoices and customers come from? Are they already stored in the client's existing .NET 8 API / Postgres database, or does this app create and own them? → assumed: Invoices and customers already exist in the client's API/database; this app reads them and adds overdue and reminder data\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\",\n   \"I-5\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-2\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Should the 7-day overdue threshold be fixed in code or a configuration setting? And how are days counted (calendar days, in which time zone)? → assumed: Configurable setting, default 7 calendar days, business time zone\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\",\n   \"I-5\",\n   \"I-6\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-3\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"What does 'days overdue' mean in the list and its filter: days since the due date, or days since the invoice was marked overdue (due date + 7)? → assumed: Days since the due date\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-5\",\n   \"I-6\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-4\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"How should the days-overdue filter work? → assumed: Preset buckets (7–30, 31–60, 60+)\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-4\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-5\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"Which email service sends reminders, and how is 'cannot be delivered' detected? → assumed: Transactional email provider (e.g. SendGrid/Postmark) with bounce webhooks; both send errors and later bounces count as failures\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-11\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-3\",\n   \"I-4\",\n   \"I-7\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-6\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Does a send attempt that fails at once (e.g. provider error, no email) still create a reminder history entry? → assumed: Yes, every attempt is logged with its outcome (sent/failed/bounced)\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-12\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-6\",\n   \"I-7\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-7\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Can staff open the invoice detail screen from the overdue list? → assumed: Yes, clicking the invoice number or row opens the detail screen\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-13\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-7\",\n   \"I-2\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-8\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Should the invoice detail screen also have a 'Send reminder' button for overdue invoices? → assumed: Yes, when the invoice is overdue\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-14\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-9\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Does the reminder email need a specific template, sender name/address, or currency format? → assumed: A simple fixed template from a configured sender address, amounts in GBP/local currency\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-10\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Should the 7-day overdue threshold be a fixed constant or a setting that can be changed? → assumed: Configurable setting, defaulting to 7 days\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\",\n   \"I-5\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-11\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Which date and timezone decide when an invoice is '7 days past due', and is 'days overdue' (used in the filter) counted from the due date or from when the invoice became overdue? → assumed: Calendar days in the business's local timezone, counted from the due date\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-4\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-12\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Which email service sends the reminders, and what sender address should they come from? → assumed: To be decided; abstract behind an interface with SMTP default\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-4\",\n   \"I-7\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-13\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"What counts as 'cannot be delivered': only errors when the email is handed to the mail service, or also later bounces and rejections? → assumed: Only immediate send errors from the mail service\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-13\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-7\",\n   \"I-2\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-14\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Should the invoice detail screen also have a 'Send reminder' button when the invoice is overdue? → assumed: Yes, same action and in-progress disabling as the list\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-14\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-15\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"What wording and format should the reminder email use, and should the amount show a currency symbol? → assumed: Fixed plain template with invoice number, amount in local currency, due date\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"cb\" kind=\"current-behaviour\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"claims\": [],\n \"header\": {\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-30T20:46:31.847Z\",\n  \"inputsHash\": \"\",\n  \"kind\": \"current-behaviour\",\n  \"producedBy\": {\n   \"stage\": \"ground\"\n  },\n  \"runId\": \"20260930-invoice-reminders-a-small-4006\",\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1\n },\n \"notFound\": [\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-1\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-2\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-3\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-4\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-5\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-6\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-7\"\n  }\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n   \"ears\": \"The invoice reminders system shall classify an invoice as overdue, working this out on every request and never storing it, only when its status in the existing system is in the configured open-status list (default ['open']), it has a due date, and the number of calendar days from its due date to today's date, both taken in the configured business time zone, is at least the configured overdue threshold (default 7).\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"Q-4\",\n    \"Q-6\",\n    \"ASM-1\",\n    \"ASM-2\",\n    \"ASM-10\",\n    \"ASM-11\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.1\",\n     \"given\": \"threshold is the default 7, business time zone Europe/London, the injected clock set to 2026-10-15, and open invoices due 2026-10-08 and 2026-10-09\",\n     \"when\": \"OverduePolicy.Evaluate is called for each invoice\",\n     \"then\": \"the call for the invoice due 2026-10-08 returns overdue = true and daysOverdue = 7, and the call for the invoice due 2026-10-09 returns overdue = false and daysOverdue = 6\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.2\",\n     \"given\": \"threshold set to 10, today 2026-10-15, and open invoices due 2026-10-07, 2026-10-06 and 2026-10-05\",\n     \"when\": \"OverduePolicy.Evaluate is called for each invoice\",\n     \"then\": \"the calls return overdue = false for the invoices due 2026-10-07 and 2026-10-06, and overdue = true for the invoice due 2026-10-05\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.3\",\n     \"given\": \"threshold 7, default open-status list ['open'], and seven invoices each 20 days past due with statuses paid, cancelled, draft, void, written-off, disputed and credited\",\n     \"when\": \"OverduePolicy.Evaluate is called for each invoice\",\n     \"then\": \"every call returns overdue = false\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.4\",\n     \"given\": \"threshold 7 and an invoice with status 'open' and a null due date\",\n     \"when\": \"OverduePolicy.Evaluate is called for it\",\n     \"then\": \"the call returns overdue = false and throws no exception\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.5\",\n     \"given\": \"business time zone Europe/London, default threshold, and an open invoice due 2026-09-01\",\n     \"when\": \"OverduePolicy.Evaluate is called at instant 2026-09-07T22:30Z (23:30 on 7 Sep local), then at 2026-09-07T23:30Z (00:30 on 8 Sep local)\",\n     \"then\": \"the first call returns daysOverdue = 6 and overdue = false, and the second returns daysOverdue = 7 and overdue = true\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.6\",\n     \"given\": \"an open invoice due 6 days ago is not in the overdue list response, and no job or data change runs\",\n     \"when\": \"the injected clock moves forward 1 day and the overdue list is requested again\",\n     \"then\": \"the response now holds the invoice with daysOverdue = 7, and the invoice record in the existing database is unchanged\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"ears\": \"When an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list, the Invoice Reminders API shall return every invoice currently classified as overdue, each with invoice ID, invoice number, customer name, amount, due date, days overdue (calendar days since the due date) and latest reminder outcome.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"I-6\",\n    \"Q-4\",\n    \"Q-6\",\n    \"ASM-1\",\n    \"ASM-3\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.1\",\n     \"given\": \"today 2026-10-15, threshold 7, and in the existing database: open invoice A for customer 'Crumb & Co' with amount 125.50 due 2026-10-01, open invoice B due 2026-10-12, invoice C due 2026-09-01 with status paid, and invoice D due 2026-09-01 with status cancelled\",\n     \"when\": \"an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list\",\n     \"then\": \"the response is 200 and holds only invoice A, with its invoice number, customer 'Crumb & Co', amount 125.50, due date 2026-10-01 and daysOverdue 14\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.2\",\n     \"given\": \"invoice A is in the overdue list\",\n     \"when\": \"its status in the existing system is changed to paid and the overdue list is requested again\",\n     \"then\": \"invoice A is no longer in the response and no overdue flag was written to the invoice record\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.3\",\n     \"given\": \"overdue invoice A with no reminder attempts and overdue invoice E whose latest attempt failed\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list is requested\",\n     \"then\": \"the response shows invoice A with latest reminder outcome null and invoice E with latest reminder outcome 'failed'\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n   \"ears\": \"When the overdue list is requested with a customer filter, the Invoice Reminders API shall return only the overdue invoices that belong to that customer.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"Q-1\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.1\",\n     \"given\": \"customer X has 2 overdue invoices, customer Y has 1 overdue invoice, and customer Z has none\",\n     \"when\": \"an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list with customerId = X, then with customerId = Z\",\n     \"then\": \"the first response holds exactly customer X's 2 invoices and the second response is 200 with an empty list\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n   \"ears\": \"When the overdue list is requested with a days-overdue bucket filter, the Invoice Reminders API shall return only overdue invoices whose days overdue fall inside the named fixed bucket (7–30, 31–60 or 61+, limits inclusive, not shifted by the configured overdue threshold), or respond 400 with a validation error when the bucket value is not one of these.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"ASM-3\",\n    \"ASM-4\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.1\",\n     \"given\": \"default threshold 7 and overdue invoices at 7, 30, 31, 60, 61 and 90 days overdue\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list is requested with bucket 7–30, then 31–60, then 61+\",\n     \"then\": \"the responses hold {7, 30}, {31, 60} and {61, 90}\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.2\",\n     \"given\": \"customers X and Y each have overdue invoices at 10 and 45 days\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list is requested with customerId = X and bucket 31–60, then with customerId = X and bucket 7–30\",\n     \"then\": \"the first response holds only X's 45-day invoice and the second holds only X's 10-day invoice\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.3\",\n     \"given\": \"any overdue invoices\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list is requested with an unknown bucket value such as '5-6'\",\n     \"then\": \"the response is 400 with a validation error naming the bucket parameter\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.4\",\n     \"given\": \"the overdue threshold is set to 5 and an open invoice is 6 days past due\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list is requested without a bucket, then with bucket 7–30, 31–60 and 61+\",\n     \"then\": \"the invoice is in the unfiltered response and is in none of the three bucket responses\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-7\",\n   \"ears\": \"When an authenticated staff user requests a reminder for an overdue invoice whose customer has a billing email, the Invoice Reminders API shall send one email through the configured email sender to that billing email, from the configured sender address, using the fixed template that contains the invoice number, the amount in local currency and the due date.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"Q-1\",\n    \"Q-2\",\n    \"ASM-9\",\n    \"ASM-12\",\n    \"ASM-15\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.1\",\n     \"given\": \"overdue invoice INV-1042 with amount 245.50, due 2026-10-01, whose customer has billing email accounts@bakery.example, and a stub email sender that accepts messages\",\n     \"when\": \"an authenticated staff user calls the send-reminder endpoint for INV-1042\",\n     \"then\": \"the response is 2xx with outcome 'sent', and the stub receives exactly one message addressed only to accounts@bakery.example, from the configured sender address, whose body contains 'INV-1042', '£245.50' and the due date in the configured date format\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-8\",\n   \"ears\": \"If a reminder is requested for an overdue invoice whose customer has no billing email, then the Invoice Reminders API shall send no email, reject the request with a 'missing billing email' error, and record the attempt in the reminder history as failed.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-2\",\n    \"Q-8\",\n    \"ASM-6\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.1\",\n     \"given\": \"an overdue invoice whose customer's billing email is null or empty, and a stub email sender\",\n     \"when\": \"an authenticated staff user calls the send-reminder endpoint for it\",\n     \"then\": \"the response is 422 with error code 'missing_billing_email' and a message saying the billing email is missing, the stub receives no message, and one reminder history row exists for the invoice with outcome 'failed' and reason 'missing billing email'\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-9\",\n   \"ears\": \"If a reminder is requested for an invoice that exists but is not overdue, including a paid or cancelled invoice, then the Invoice Reminders API shall reject the request with a 409 error, send no email and add no reminder history entry.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"Q-4\",\n    \"ASM-1\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.1\",\n     \"given\": \"threshold 7, an open invoice INV-1050 that is 3 days past due, an invoice INV-1051 with status paid that is 40 days past due, and a stub email sender\",\n     \"when\": \"an authenticated staff user calls the send-reminder endpoint for INV-1050, then for INV-1051\",\n     \"then\": \"both responses are 409 with an error saying the invoice is not overdue, the stub receives no message, and no reminder history row exists for either invoice\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-10\",\n   \"ears\": \"When a reminder send attempt for an overdue invoice finishes, the Invoice Reminders API shall add one row to the reminder history table in the Postgres database holding the invoice ID, the ID of the authenticated staff user who sent it, the server UTC timestamp of the attempt, the outcome (sent or failed) and the failure reason when there is one.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"Q-1\",\n    \"Q-7\",\n    \"Q-8\",\n    \"ASM-6\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.1\",\n     \"given\": \"staff user 'jane' is authenticated, overdue invoice INV-1 has no reminder history, and the stub email sender succeeds\",\n     \"when\": \"jane sends a reminder for INV-1 at 2026-10-15T09:00:00Z\",\n     \"then\": \"exactly one history row exists for INV-1 with jane's user ID as sender, timestamp 2026-10-15T09:00:00Z (±5 s), outcome 'sent' and no failure reason\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.2\",\n     \"given\": \"INV-1 already has one 'sent' history row\",\n     \"when\": \"staff user 'tom' sends another reminder for INV-1\",\n     \"then\": \"two rows exist for INV-1, the first row is unchanged, and the new row has tom's user ID as sender\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-11\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Invoice Reminders API shall answer every request to edit or delete a reminder history entry with HTTP 404 or 405 and leave the entry unchanged.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-3\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.1\",\n     \"given\": \"an invoice with one reminder history entry with a known ID\",\n     \"when\": \"an authenticated staff user sends PUT, PATCH and DELETE requests to the invoice's reminders collection path and to that entry's path\",\n     \"then\": \"each response is 404 or 405 and the entry's row in the database is unchanged\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-12\",\n   \"ears\": \"When an authenticated staff user requests an invoice's details, the Invoice Reminders API shall return the invoice number, customer name, amount, due date, overdue flag, days overdue, the latest reminder outcome taken from the newest history entry, and the full reminder history newest first, with each entry's sender, timestamp, outcome and failure reason.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"I-7\",\n    \"Q-8\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.1\",\n     \"given\": \"overdue invoice INV-1042 with attempts failed on 2026-10-10 by u-17 (reason 'SMTP 554'), then sent on 2026-10-12 by u-20\",\n     \"when\": \"an authenticated staff user requests INV-1042's details\",\n     \"then\": \"the response holds amount, due date, overdue = true, latest outcome 'sent', and the history with the 2026-10-12 entry (u-20, sent) first and the 2026-10-10 entry (u-17, failed, 'SMTP 554') second\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.2\",\n     \"given\": \"an overdue invoice with no reminder history\",\n     \"when\": \"its details are requested\",\n     \"then\": \"the response has an empty history list and latest outcome null\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-13\",\n   \"ears\": \"If the email sender returns an error when a reminder is handed to it, then the Invoice Reminders API shall return an error response with outcome 'failed' and the error reason, record the attempt as failed with the sender's error message as the reason, and keep the invoice in the overdue list.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"Q-8\",\n    \"ASM-13\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.1\",\n     \"given\": \"overdue invoice INV-1042 with a billing email, and a stub email sender set to throw 'SMTP 554 rejected'\",\n     \"when\": \"an authenticated staff user calls the send-reminder endpoint\",\n     \"then\": \"the response is 502 and reports outcome 'failed' with a reason containing 'SMTP 554 rejected', and a history row with outcome 'failed' and that reason is stored\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.2\",\n     \"given\": \"the failed attempt in AC-13.1 has happened\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list and the invoice details are requested\",\n     \"then\": \"INV-1042 is still in the overdue list response with latest reminder outcome 'failed', and the details response shows latest outcome 'failed' with reason containing 'SMTP 554 rejected'\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-14\",\n   \"ears\": \"If a request to any Invoice Reminders endpoint has no valid staff authentication from the existing API, then the Invoice Reminders API shall reject it with HTTP 401 without returning invoice data, sending email or changing data.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-1\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.1\",\n     \"given\": \"no token, and separately an expired token\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list, invoice detail and send-reminder endpoints are called\",\n     \"then\": \"each response is 401 with no invoice or customer data in the body, the stub email sender receives no message, and no history row is added\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.2\",\n     \"given\": \"a valid token for any staff user with no special role\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list, invoice detail and send-reminder endpoints are called for an overdue invoice with a billing email\",\n     \"then\": \"none returns 401 or 403 and each succeeds (2xx)\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-18\",\n   \"ears\": \"If an invoice detail or send-reminder request names an invoice ID that does not exist in the existing system, then the Invoice Reminders API shall respond with HTTP 404, send no email and add no reminder history row.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-7\",\n    \"ASM-1\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-18.1\",\n     \"given\": \"no invoice with ID 999999 exists in the existing database\",\n     \"when\": \"an authenticated staff user requests GET /api/invoices/999999\",\n     \"then\": \"the response is 404 and its body holds no invoice or customer data\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-18.2\",\n     \"given\": \"no invoice with ID 999999 exists and a stub email sender is configured\",\n     \"when\": \"an authenticated staff user calls POST /api/invoices/999999/reminders\",\n     \"then\": \"the response is 404, the stub receives no message, and no reminder history row with invoice ID 999999 exists\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.3333333333333333\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n   \"text\": \"The overdue list endpoint meets the stated latency at the stated data volumes, with or without filters.\",\n   \"metric\": \"p95 ≤ 1,000 ms at the API with 10,000 invoices (at least 5,000 of them open) and 50,000 reminder history rows, with or without filters\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n   \"text\": \"The send-reminder endpoint waits a limited time for the email sender and records a timeout as a failed attempt.\",\n   \"metric\": \"Email sender call times out after 10 s; endpoint responds within 12 s in 100% of calls; a timeout creates a 'failed' history row\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-3\",\n   \"text\": \"Customer PII (billing email addresses), invoice amounts and reminder email bodies are kept out of application logs.\",\n   \"metric\": \"0 customer billing email addresses or reminder email bodies found in application log output across the whole automated acceptance test run\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-4\",\n   \"text\": \"All Invoice Reminders endpoints require authentication.\",\n   \"metric\": \"100% of new Invoice Reminders endpoints return 401 without a valid token (checked by an automated endpoint sweep)\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-5\",\n   \"text\": \"Reminder history is durable and append-only: the application never removes or changes history rows.\",\n   \"metric\": \"0 UPDATE or DELETE statements against the reminder history table in application code (static check); 0 history rows lost or changed across the test run and after 1,000 back-to-back send attempts that include 100 forced email-sender failures\"\n  }\n ],\n \"outOfScope\": [\n  \"Run 2 of the sequence (not this run): building the React overdue list screen (table, customer and bucket filters, per-row 'Send reminder' button, link to detail) and invoice detail screen (amount, due date, history, failures, 'Send reminder' button while overdue) described in I-6 and I-7; this run delivers only the API data and actions those screens use\",\n  \"Run 2 of the sequence (not this run): disabling the 'Send reminder' button while a send is in progress (Q-5, ASM-14) and showing the send result on screen\",\n  \"Payments and recording payments (paid/cancelled status is only read from the existing system)\",\n  \"Customer logins or any customer-facing screens\",\n  \"SMS reminders\",\n  \"Detecting delivery failures after hand-off (bounces, complaint/provider webhooks, later rejections); only immediate email-sender errors count as failures (ASM-13)\",\n  \"Automatic or scheduled reminders; every send is started by staff\",\n  \"A stored 'overdue' status on the invoice or a daily job to set it; overdue is computed at query time (Q-6)\",\n  \"Server-side duplicate-send protection (cooldown, daily limit, duplicate check) (Q-5)\",\n  \"Role-based permissions beyond 'any authenticated staff user' (Q-1)\",\n  \"Creating or editing invoices, customers or billing emails (ASM-1)\",\n  \"Sending to more than one contact per customer (Q-2)\",\n  \"Editing or deleting reminder history entries (Q-3)\",\n  \"Configurable email templates or wording (ASM-9, ASM-15)\",\n  \"Days-overdue buckets that move with the configured threshold; buckets are fixed at 7–30, 31–60, 61+\"\n ],\n \"assumptions\": [\n  \"Run sequence: the spec was over the feature size budget, so the work is split. Run 1 (this spec) covers the API: overdue rule, list, filters, send, history, detail, auth and unknown-invoice handling. Run 2 covers the React screens (old REQ-15, REQ-16, REQ-17), which are kept under suggestions.\",\n  \"The bucket conflict is settled in favour of fixed buckets (old REQ-5, 2 of 3 drafts, matches ASM-4's literal 7–30 / 31–60 / 60+). The rule is now part of REQ-4 (AC-4.4). Old REQ-6 (lowest bucket starts at the threshold) is dropped. If the threshold is set below 7, invoices overdue by fewer than 7 days appear only in the unfiltered list.\",\n  \"The existing .NET 8 API / Postgres schema was not available to check (current-behaviour: 'no repository: this is new build work'). These are logical fields that must be mapped to the client's real schema and confirmed before build: invoice status values (open, paid, cancelled and others), a single customer billing email field, customer name, invoice number and amount fields, and the claim in the existing auth token that holds the staff user ID. Test data is seeded through the confirmed schema.\",\n  \"An invoice can be overdue only if its existing-system status is in a configured open-status allow-list (default ['open'], to be confirmed against the client's status values). Any other status (paid, cancelled, draft, void, written-off, disputed, credited, or unknown) and any null due date is never overdue. Q-4 still holds: paid and cancelled invoices drop off automatically.\",\n  \"ASM-13 is used over ASM-5: 'cannot be delivered' means only an immediate error from the email sender, plus a missing billing email. Bounce webhooks (ASM-5, high risk) must be confirmed by the product owner before build. ASM-6's 'bounced' outcome is not used, so outcomes are 'sent' or 'failed'.\",\n  \"ASM-12 is used over ASM-5 for the provider: sending goes through an email-sender interface with an SMTP default, and tests use a stub/fake of that interface.\",\n  \"Invoices, customers, billing emails and paid/cancelled status are read from the client's existing .NET 8 API / Postgres database (ASM-1). The only new table is reminder history, keyed by invoice ID (Q-7).\",\n  \"The overdue threshold is configurable with a default of 7. An invoice is overdue when today's local date in the configured business time zone (Europe/London in the examples) minus the due date is at least the threshold. 'Days overdue' means calendar days since the due date (ASM-2, ASM-3, ASM-10, ASM-11).\",\n  \"ASM-4's '60+' bucket is read as 61+ so it does not overlap 31–60. Bucket limits are inclusive.\",\n  \"Today's date comes from an injectable clock so tests can fix it. Day counting lives in one policy class (OverduePolicy) that takes the clock, threshold, open-status list and time zone.\",\n  \"A send blocked by a missing billing email counts as an attempt and is logged as failed (Q-8, ASM-6). A send for an existing invoice that is not overdue is rejected with no history entry.\",\n  \"Status codes: 401 unauthenticated, 404 unknown invoice ID, 409 not overdue, 422 missing billing email, 502 email sender error, 400 invalid bucket, 404/405 for history edit/delete attempts.\",\n  \"The reminder uses a fixed plain template from a configured sender address. The amount is shown in GBP with a £ symbol (e.g. '£245.50'). The date format in the email is set in config.\",\n  \"'Who sent it' is the user ID from the existing API's authentication token (Q-1).\",\n  \"A successful send does not take an invoice off the overdue list. Only a status outside the open-status list in the existing system does (Q-4, Q-6).\",\n  \"Proposed API paths: GET /api/invoices/overdue?customerId=&daysOverdue={bucket}, GET /api/invoices/{id}, POST /api/invoices/{id}/reminders.\",\n  \"NFR-1 uses the largest data volume any draft gave. NFR-2 uses the stricter 10 s / 12 s limits.\"\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\nReview the spec."}